  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FD21BC">Definition <span data-tag="FD21BC">2.2.3.2</span>.</a>pointwise equivalenceequivalence!pointwise Suppose given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [rr]^{f} \ar [dr]^{p} &  &  Y \ar [dl]^{q} \\ &  S, &  } \]
</div>
  <p> where $p$ and $q$ are right fibrations. We will say that $f$ is a <em>pointwise equivalence</em> if, for each vertex $s \in S$, the induced map $X_{s} \rightarrow Y_{s}$ is a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes. </p>
